# vehje-codegen — backlog

## Deferred target implementations (each a follow-up round)

### NativeTarget — real Rust/LLVM codegen

Replace the skeleton empty-artifact `emit` body with a real Rust
or LLVM-IR (via `inkwell` or `cranelift`) lowering path. Requires
the target-agnostic IR + lowering passes (below).

### JominiTarget — Clausewitz engine bytecode

Move `JominiTarget` out of vehje-codegen into a sibling
`vehje-jomini` repo with its own mockspace, implementing the
real Clausewitz script emission for Paradox games. Bind targets:
Country, Pop, Planet, etc. (per stellar-heritage Python prior
art). Landing in its own `orgrinrt/vehje-jomini` GitHub repo.

### Possible future targets
- WebAssembly backend.
- Python bytecode (parity-oracle / transpile path).
- Lua script emission (future `vehje-lua`).

## Deferred framework features

### IR lowering

Resolved → internal IR → target-specific lowering. The skeleton
passes `Resolved` directly to the target; a future round
introduces the target-agnostic IR layer so backends don't each
re-walk the AST.

### Optimisation passes

Passes between IR and codegen: inlining, constant folding,
dead-code elimination. Shared across all targets.

### Target-specific diagnostics

Per-target error recovery. Currently `CodegenError` is a flat
enum; targets that need to surface multi-phase diagnostics will
want a dedicated per-target error rendering path (R3's
`render_diagnostic(err: &TargetError) -> Diagnostic`).

### Per-target config

`Vehje.toml` `[codegen.target_name]` subsection read by the
driver and passed through `CodegenCtx`.

### Incremental codegen

Cache artifacts by IR hash so unchanged units skip re-emission.
Requires the artefact-cache reference in `CodegenCtx` (R3 shape).

### R3-shape retrofit

Associated `NAME` / `VERSION` consts, `accepts(kind)` routing,
`stages()` pipeline entry, `CodegenOutput` with `manifest` +
`references`, `render_diagnostic`. Lands once real backend
bodies surface the need — the instance-method skeleton form is
forward-compatible (retrofit requires no consumer changes).

## Non-blocking follow-ups

### Extension loading

Dynamic targets via `dlopen` / DLL (so `vehje-jomini` ships as
a runtime plugin the Vehje driver picks up). Requires a stable
C-ABI wrapper around `CodegenTarget`.

### Cross-compilation target triples

`NativeTarget` grows a triple parameter (e.g. `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`
vs `aarch64-apple-darwin`) driven by CLI `--target-triple`.

### Debug info emission

DWARF / CodeView generation per backend. Requires lowered IR to
preserve source spans.

### Stage reordering via topological sort

Current R3 `Stage` enum fixes the five-stage order (PreTypecheck
→ PostTypecheck → CodegenPre → Codegen → Link). If a target
needs "my stage X must happen before target Y's stage Z", the
schedule crate grows a target-stage dep resolver. Defer until a
concrete multi-target workflow surfaces the need.

### Target-provided lints

Targets may want to emit target-specific warnings during codegen
(e.g. Clausewitz-only "this pattern will OOM Stellaris at
runtime"). Current Diagnostic flow handles this via severity
tagging; a dedicated "lint scope" annotation could help IDEs
filter target-specific noise. Defer until a target surfaces real
need.

### SymbolRef cross-target resolution

R3 ships `SymbolRef` as the opaque type that targets use to
reference symbols across boundaries (vehje-jomini references
vehje-builtin symbols, etc.). The resolution ALGORITHM
(link-stage walker that matches SymbolRef producers ↔ consumers)
is deferred — first vehje-jomini release will likely go without
cross-target references, and the algorithm lands when a concrete
need arrives.

### Multi-target parallel codegen

Current design is sequential: compile all units with target A,
then target B, etc. Parallel-codegen across targets (for
tooling-friendly UX) is a future optimisation — needs shared
ArtefactCache locking story.

## Post-review notes

### Manual DiagPhase labelling on every Diagnostic

`DiagPhase` is not enforced at the `CodegenTarget` trait level.
Implementors must manually pass `DiagPhase::Codegen` on every
`Diagnostic::new` / `Diagnostic::error` call site when they
start producing real diagnostics in their `emit` body. The
compiler cannot catch a codegen target that labels its
diagnostics `DiagPhase::Typecheck` by mistake.

When the `DiagnosticSink` retrofit lands (R3 trait-shape BACKLOG
entry above, pointing at the `render_diagnostic(err: &TargetError)
-> Diagnostic` surface), its constructor should accept a
`DiagPhase` and stamp every pushed diagnostic automatically.
That removes the manual-labelling obligation and the class of
mis-label bugs with it.

Until that retrofit lands, target authors must keep the phase
tag consistent by convention.
